  "steps": [
    "Marinate the chicken: Pat dry 2 pounds chicken thighs with paper towels. Season with 1 teaspoon kosher salt (for chicken) and 1/2 teaspoon black pepper (for chicken). Whisk together 1/2 cup harissa (for chicken), 5 garlic cloves, minced (for chicken), 1/2 teaspoon lemon zest, 2 tablespoons lemon juice (for chicken), and 1/3 cup honey (for chicken). Toss chicken in the marinade, cover, and refrigerate.",
    "Preheat oven: Place a rack in the center of the oven and preheat to 400°F / 204°C. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "Bake chicken: Arrange marinated chicken on the baking sheet. Brush with any leftover sauce. Bake until internal temp reaches 165°F.",
    "Rest and cut chicken: Cover chicken with foil and rest. Then cut into bite-sized cubes.",
    "Cook the rice: Bring 2 cups water or stock, 1 tablespoon olive oil (for rice), and 1 teaspoon kosher salt (for rice) to a boil in a saucepan. Add 1 cup brown jasmine rice, rinsed, return to a boil, then cover and reduce heat to low. Simmer without peeking.",
    "Rest the rice: Turn off heat and let rice rest with the lid on. Then fluff with a fork and season with 1/2 teaspoon black pepper (for rice) and 1 tablespoon parsley, chopped.",
    "Make the vinaigrette: Combine 1/3 cup olive oil (for vinaigrette), 3 tablespoons lemon juice (for vinaigrette), 2 tablespoons harissa (for vinaigrette), 1 tablespoon honey (for vinaigrette), 1 garlic clove, minced (for vinaigrette), 1/2 teaspoon kosher salt (for vinaigrette), and 1/4 teaspoon black pepper (for vinaigrette) in a mason jar. Shake until emulsified, about 30 seconds . Adjust seasoning to taste.",
    "Assemble bowls: Divide rice among bowls. Top with 6 cups salad greens, chicken, 1 cup cucumbers, diced, 1 cup cherry tomatoes, halved, 1/2 cup pickled red onions, 1 cup Kalamata olives, and 1 cup corn (grilled or canned). Add dollops of 1 cup hummus, 1 cup tzatziki, and 1/2 cup feta cheese, crumbled. Drizzle with vinaigrette and serve with 1 pita chips (optional)."
  ],
